<Page title="Contact Allemojipedia" description="Contact the Allemojipedia editorial team to report an error, suggest an emoji meaning, ask about the site or raise a privacy or copyright concern." path="/contact/" keywords={["contact allemojipedia"]} heading="Contact Allemojipedia" lead="Corrections, suggestions and questions are all welcome.">
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>General questions and partnerships: <a href="mailto:contact@allemojipedia.com">contact@allemojipedia.com</a></p>
  <p>Corrections and feedback on a page: <a href="mailto:feedback@allemojipedia.com">feedback@allemojipedia.com</a></p>

  <h2>Reporting an error</h2>
  <p>To help us fix a mistake quickly, please include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the address of the page,</li>
    <li>the sentence or detail you think is wrong, and</li>
    <li>what you believe is correct, with a source if you have one.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We read every report. Our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> describes how corrections are handled.</p>

  <h2>Suggesting an emoji or a guide</h2>
  <p>If an emoji you care about does not have its own meaning page yet, or you would like a guide on a topic we have not covered, let us know which one and why it matters to you. Requests help us decide what to write next.</p>

  <h2>Privacy and copyright</h2>
  <p>For privacy requests, see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and write to the contact address above. Emoji artwork belongs to the platform that designed it; this site displays your device's own emoji font and does not host vendor emoji images. If you believe any content here infringes your rights, email us with the details and we will respond.</p>

  <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>
  <p>We cannot add emojis to your phone or to the Unicode Standard. New emojis are approved by the Unicode Consortium; our guide on <a href="/guides/how-new-emojis-get-approved/">how new emojis get approved</a> explains the process.</p>
</Page>
